# macOS signing identity. NEVER commit any of this.
#
# The .p12 (and its .base64 form) contains the PRIVATE KEY. Anyone who has it
# can sign a Paseo build that every installed copy will download and install by
# itself, silently. That is not a hypothetical: the whole point of pinning a
# certificate is that any build signed with it is accepted as an update.
#
# The certificate alone (cert.pem) is public information — it is embedded in
# every .app this repo ships, and anyone can extract it with
# `codesign -d --extract-certificates`. That one is harmless. The private key is
# not.
mac-signing-cert/
*.p12
*.p12.base64
*.keychain-db
